{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169139-errata-thread-w20-changing-ways","id":1169139,"title":"Errata Thread: W20 Changing Ways","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-20T10:59:07-08:00","id":1169139,"title":"Errata Thread: W20 Changing Ways","content":"This thread is for capturing errata, including typos, mechanical inconsistencies, misplaced graphical elements, etc. for Changing Ways.<br /> <br /> Questions and other general discussion should go in another thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-20T16:45:09-08:00","id":1169222,"title":"","content":"It seems like there was a font problem starting around page 34 where all uses of the letters a and s were bolded, which went on for some time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-22T07:10:28-08:00","id":1169625,"title":"","content":"<b>p.89-90. </b>There is mention of Black Fury homid males in this paragraph. According to W20 p.80, any male garou from their tribe, that is not a metis, is sent to another tribe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T13:21:34-08:00","id":1169992,"title":"","content":"<b>Go for the Jugular:</b> Page 151...unsoakable bite attack for only 1 point of Rage with no roll other then a diff 5 bite attack, and only at rank 2? Seems a little over kill to me. Especially when you compare it to Rank 5<b> Fenris' Bite</b> that only does 3 unsoakable agg (plus any bite dmg rolled) to a limb and requires expending a Rage plus a roll with the diff being the opponent's stamina+3.<br /> <br /> Maybe if it cost a gnosis and just doubled your bite dmg? That would still be extremely useful but not put a Rank 5 gift to shame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 12-23-2017, 04:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T05:47:16-08:00","id":1170153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1169139-errata-thread-w20-changing-ways?p=1169992#post1169992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Go for the Jugular:</b> Page 151...unsoakable bite attack for only 1 point of Rage with no roll other then a diff 5 bite attack, and only at rank 2? Seems a little over kill to me. Especially when you compare it to Rank 5<b> Fenris' Bite</b> that only does 3 unsoakable agg (plus any bite dmg rolled) to a limb and requires expending a Rage plus a roll with the diff being the opponent's stamina+3.<br /> <br /> Maybe if it cost a gnosis and just doubled your bite dmg? That would still be extremely useful but not put a Rank 5 gift to shame.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or just replace the Fenris bite with this awesomeness (haven't read the book yet) but IMHO Fenris Bite as it is written allows you to automatically hit an enemy limb (maybe head too, potentially one shot kill any head you can reach) with a difficulty 5 bite attack and without the need to declare a called shot. It also does +3 automatic unsoakable aggravater damage additionally to the successes you may achieve in a damage roll. <br /> <br /> Even Bachante's Rage as a rank 3 is more costly and you need to allready pass damage to a character in order to then spend Rage for extra unsoakable damage and spend a Gnosis in order to activate the gift for the scene.<br /> <br /> So a Rank 2 gift that does aggravated unsoakable with just one Rage is too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T04:38:47-08:00","id":1170649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Changing Ways, ch.3, p.72-73</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b> Nervous Transformation</b><br /> You were born in Crinos shape and you instinctively seek to return to this shape whenever you are in danger. Whenever you are intimidated, threatened, attacked, or feel you are in danger, roll Willpower (difficulty 8) to avoid instantly assuming Crinos shape. You cannot shift out of Crinos until the threat has passed, though if the situation changes you can try to shift to another form by rolling Willpower again.</div> </div> </div> </div>This should be a flaw rather than a deformity. Given all metis have Crinos as their birthform and all still share the farmiliar want to feel safe, it doesn't stand out, It also doesn't stand out as something -wrong- with the garou in a deep level, just a 'eesh, danger!' reaction. Which falls under the flaw 'Forced Transformation'.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T22:39:02-08:00","id":1171461,"title":"","content":"The gift &quot;Battle Cry&quot; on page 154-155, I'm unclear on what the bonus dice are for. Is it for all rolls for an entire scene? round? Is it bonus dice to initiative? Might just be me but I was unclear","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T07:04:25-08:00","id":1171525,"title":"","content":"Page 20 says &quot;Event Metis&quot; instead of &quot;Even Metis&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-29T19:23:35-08:00","id":1171694,"title":"","content":"The Lupus gift Hibernate on pages 151-152 says that a Garou who wakes up from hibernation must roll frenzy at a +1 diff, and +2 if they were injured. Does that mean waking from hibernation is meant to be harder to frenzy then normal, especially if they were woken up by being injured? Or did the book mean to post -1 and -2?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-30T18:45:57-08:00","id":1171935,"title":"","content":"Rally the Troops-Page 150: It says that you get bonus dice to rolls involving a set task. Let's say that roll is to get a group of people to attack some enemy...does that mean the Garou using the gift gets bonus dice to brawl but the people aiding him don't? I just want to make sure the bonus dice were intended to be for the player using the gift only, and not the crowd they are calling on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}